# Todoer — CLI Task Management Application

A command-line Python application for managing to-do tasks with persistent storage in a MySQL / MariaDB database.

---

## 📁 Project Structure

```text
├── todoer/
│   ├── .env            # Local environment variables (git-ignored)
│   ├── init_db.py      # Database table initialization script
│   └── todoer.py       # Main application script
├── .env.example        # Environment configuration template
├── .gitignore          # Git ignore rules (venv, .env, __pycache__)
├── requirements.txt    # Project dependencies
└── README.md           # Project documentation
```

## Create and activate a virtual environment:

Windows (PowerShell):

PowerShell
```bash
python -m venv venv
.\venv\Scripts\activate
```
Linux / macOS:

```Bash
python3 -m venv venv
source venv/bin/activate
```
Install dependencies:

```Bash
pip install -r requirements.txt
```
## ⚙️ Configuration
Copy .env.example to create .env inside the todoer/ directory:

```Bash
cp .env.example todoer/.env
```
## 🚀 Running the Application
Database Table Initialization (First-time setup):
If the target table does not exist on the remote server yet, execute the initialization script:

```Bash
python todoer/init_db.py
```
Launch Main Application:

```bash
python todoer/todoer.py
```